 1             II.      ASSIGNMENT AND SUMMARY OF TESTIMONY

 2   Q.   What is your assignment in this testimony?

 3   A.   I am providing testimony in support of the Comprehensive Stipulation

 4        (“Stipulation”), and specifically Section 1.2 related to depreciation rates,

 5        depreciation expense, and service lives of generating assets. I am also providing

 6        testimony demonstrating that Section 1.2 meets the New Mexico Public Regulation

 7        Commission’s (“Commission”) criteria for reviewing the reasonableness of a

 8        settlement.

 9   Q.   Please summarize your testimony and overall recommendations.

10   A.   I recommend the Commission approve the depreciation-related portion of the

11        Stipulation because it represents a reasonable compromise by the Signatories,

12        provides New Mexico customers with a number of benefits compared to a fully

13        litigated outcome, and is in the public interest. With respect to depreciation, the

14        Stipulation allows SPS to recover its capital investments in a timely manner over

15        agreed-upon service lives, while helping to mitigate the effect of the rate increase

16        on New Mexico retail customers. Further, I specifically discuss how Section 1.2

17        serves the public interest and is consistent with standard ratemaking practice.




